# Keep the build context to source only.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` copies whatever the developer happens to have on
# their machine into the image - most damagingly the host `node_modules`, which
# would overwrite the Linux modules installed inside the container with
# platform-specific ones (Windows/arm64 binaries in a Debian image).
node_modules
dist
coverage

# Secrets never belong in an image layer. The variables this app needs are
# supplied at runtime by compose (`env_file` + `environment`), so the image
# does not need them, and baking them in would leak them to anyone who can
# pull the image regardless of what .gitignore says.
.env
.env.local

*.log
.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile
